--- Ada's diary ---
I scrubbed offices from seven to nine o'clock this morning, and found a half-crown under Mr. Hale's desk. I was pleased, and went happily to my work in Finsbury Circus.

--- Arthur's diary ---
I waited till a quarter past nine. Then I went to the clerks' room, and Mr. Thomas spoke to me. He said, "Hale, I am sorry to hear you have been unwell; but you mustn't give way to it. Cheer up, man, cheer up." I thanked him, and said I hoped to be all right soon.

